scope one red closed, one page cited, no new guard
status GREEN -- log_has_a_row and index_row_bound both GREEN on metal after the repair; cold roster 204 guards, 200 green, 2 gated at %5, the one red being this lap's own subject; hot pass named in the send
obs Against the tree: this is the third recorded firing of the shelf-link depth fault in two days, always at the moment a card block is copied into an archive shelf. A REDS fold has a tool that repoints; an account shelf has the repointer and no gesture that calls it. Named rather than built, since the ledger pin holds 173 bytes and a row has nowhere to go.
recommend keep-going -- the next docs-geode lap can ask whether a page's CLAIM should name what holds it still, the way Gauge already asks it of a figure; the answer decides whether this becomes a meter or stays a habit
